{"name":"Menthol","hex":"#c1f9a2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"menthol","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cyclic monoterpene alcohol; the major component of the essential oil of peppermint; used in pharmaceutical preparations as an antitussive and antipruritic agent, as a nasal decongestant, and in menthol cigarettes.","A menthol cigarette."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/menthol"}],"entries":[{"title":"Menthol","blocks":[{"text":"Menthol is a monoterpenoid organic compound that occurs naturally in the oils of certain plants in the mint family, such as corn mint and peppermint. It is a white or clear waxy crystalline substance that is solid at room temperature and melts slightly above. The main form of menthol occurring in nature is (−)-menthol, which is assigned the (1R,2S,5R) configuration."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Menthol_Crystals.JPG/330px-Menthol_Crystals.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Menthol","wikidata":"Q407418"},{"title":"Menthol (data page)","blocks":[{"text":"This page provides supplementary chemical data on Menthol."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Menthol_(data_page)","wikidata":"Q6817558"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Menthol-from-xtal-1999-3D-balls.png/500px-Menthol-from-xtal-1999-3D-balls.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Menthol-from-xtal-1999-3D-balls.png/1280px-Menthol-from-xtal-1999-3D-balls.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Menthol-from-xtal-1999-3D-balls.png/500px-Menthol-from-xtal-1999-3D-balls.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ball-and-stick model of (−)